# Licence snapshots and vendored fixtures are captured VERBATIM and must never be
# line-ending normalised. The whole point of a snapshot is showing exactly what an upstream
# said; a CRLF file rewritten to LF is no longer that, and the difference is invisible in a
# diff viewer. Twenty-four spine licence files silently drifted to LF this way before the
# guard existed — ingest kept producing the correct bytes and git kept normalising them back.
licenses/** -text
vendor/** -text

# Locks are generated JSON; treat them as data rather than merge candidates.
locks/*.lock.json -text -diff
